    "lawCode": "Add §3003-b, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4085\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to availability of\nair transport ambulance service providers to store and distribute blood\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends public health law to add a new section to allow for air\ntransport ambulances to store and distribute blood. Distribution of the\nblood is limited to only a registered nurse on the aircraft.  The new\nsection also sets forth the standards of care that air transport ambu-\nlances must adhere to when handling, storing and distributing the blood.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAir ambulance services often need to transfuse blood products in order\nto resuscitate a patient during transport. However, regulations in this\nstate do not allow air ambulance services to do so without becoming an\nAmbulance Transfusion Service which, among other barriers, requires a\nwritten agreement between the air ambulance and the hospital blood bank\nthat provides the blood products for the patient. Obtaining written\nagreements with each hospital blood bank can be impracticable. Moreover,\nthis regulation only allows for transfusion during transport between\nhospitals, and does not provide for any ambulance to carry its own blood\nproducts to administer to patientshemorrhagic shock.  New York is the\nonly state that does not currently allow for air ambulance services to\ntransfuse blood products. This bill would put New York on par with every\nother state and allow air ambulances to carry their own blood. products\nand transfuse patients in hemorrhagic shock. These critical care medical\nproviders, practicing in the unique healthcare environment of air ambu-\nlances, have an opportunity to save the lives of the citizens of New\nYork.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: 58346 HEALTH / A11116 health\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
