  "chapter": 779,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 135 Chapter 779\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4085-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to availability\n        of air  transport  ambulance  service  providers  to  store  and\n        distribute blood\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation authorizes air transport ambulance service providers\nto store and distribute blood, and initiate and administer blood  trans-\nfusions.\n \n  This  bill will improve our emergency response and help save the lives\nof New Yorkers. However, I have secured an agreement with  the  Legisla-\nture  to ensure that air transport ambulance service providers store and\nadminister blood products in accordance with the State's  safety  stand-\nards  and regulations. Pursuant to this agreement, the ambulance service\nprovider must provide prior notification to the Department of Health  of\nits  intent to store and distribute blood. With those necessary changes,\nI am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign the bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
